{
	"version": 5,
	"id": "Bj0PABWgeKYCL2-iE",
	"notes": "An NPC template, not a player-character build: a Combat Servitor, a lobotomized criminal or debtor grafted with a mounted weapon and heavy augmetic reinforcement, fielded as expendable, utterly obedient battlefield muscle by the Cult Mechanicus and any Militarum force it attaches to. Point math: ST 14 (+40), DX 9 (-20), IQ 6 (-80), HT 12 (+20) = -40 (Will and Per both default to IQ 6 at no extra cost); advantages +74; disadvantages -110; skills +9. Total -67 points. A negative total is expected and correct for this kind of construct-NPC stat block (the same way some GURPS bestiary write-ups price a creature built almost entirely out of disadvantages below zero): a Servitor isn't a character anyone plays, it's a thing the Mechanicus builds, and the disadvantages of having had most of a person surgically removed genuinely outweigh what's left. GMs should treat the listed HP/ST/etc. as the real numbers to fight and should not expect a player to \"buy\" this template. The mounted weapon itself (heavy bolter, flamer, etc.) is equipment, not covered here.\n",
	"traits": [
		{
			"id": "trjZQDSHArTEFusH-",
			"name": "ST",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Menial and combat Servitor stock is chosen or reinforced for raw strength; augmetic replacement adds more on top.\n\nDesign: ST 14 (+4), 10 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 40,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "st",
					"amount": 4
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tC5vdS_CP_NaXtg1s",
			"name": "DX",
			"local_notes": "Lore: What's left of fine motor control after the excision is well below the human average; a Servitor moves like the machine it now mostly is.\n\nDesign: DX 9 (-1), 20 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": -20,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "dx",
					"amount": -1
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tb5g3Qhop2lofQEW8",
			"name": "IQ",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Enough intelligence remains to follow simple binharic command-cant and standing orders; nothing more. Will and Perception both default to this IQ (6) rather than being bought up, since nothing about a Servitor calls for either to be higher.\n\nDesign: IQ 6 (-4), 20 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": -80,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "iq",
					"amount": -4
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "teejJIUXFEJlLCPrN",
			"name": "HT",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Surgical and augmetic reinforcement produce real physical endurance, whatever else was removed.\n\nDesign: HT 12 (+2), 10 pts/level (B14).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 20,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "ht",
					"amount": 2
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tQRLdHCsTqXFpaMHV",
			"name": "Mechadendrite, Ballistic Pattern",
			"reference": "B53",
			"local_notes": "Extra Arm, Weapon Mount: can aim and fire a mounted weapon (bought separately as equipment) but do nothing else — no fine manipulation, no unarmed use.\n\nLore: The mounted heavy weapon (a heavy bolter, flamer, or similar) that defines a Combat Servitor's battlefield role.\n\nDesign: Extra Arm (B53, 10) with the Weapon Mount modifier (B53, -80%): 10 x 0.2 = 2 points. The weapon it carries is a separate equipment purchase, not part of this trait.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"base_points": 2
		},
		{
			"id": "tJlozS12bny-DEscc",
			"name": "Augmetic Arm, Combat Pattern",
			"reference": "B40",
			"local_notes": "Arm ST +6 (lifting and thrust/swing damage with this arm only); DR 6 on this arm only.\n\nLore: The Servitor's other arm, reinforced for melee and heavy lifting when the mounted weapon isn't the answer.\n\nDesign: Arm ST +6 (B40, 5/level, 30) + DR 6, Partial (single limb) -60% (6x5=30, x0.4=12) = 42 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus",
				"Skitarii"
			],
			"base_points": 42
		},
		{
			"id": "tuYLaajueplXnDXmK",
			"name": "Subdermal Armour Plating",
			"reference": "B46",
			"local_notes": "DR, all locations; stacks with worn armor.\n\nLore: Ceramite or plasteel weave grafted beneath the skin across the whole body, rather than replacing a specific organ or limb — the augmetic equivalent of the Astartes' Ossmodula, bought by Tech-Priests who expect to take a hit.\n\nDesign: Plain Damage Resistance (B46), 5 points/level, no location restriction since it covers the whole body. Bought here at a default 2 levels (DR 10, 10 points); raise or lower the level to taste.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"points_per_level": 5,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 2
		},
		{
			"id": "tuv3XuI8Dk_PC0sBp",
			"name": "Respirator Plugs (Filtration Lungs)",
			"reference": "B55",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Grille-covered intake valves set into the throat or chest, scrubbing forge smog, promethium fumes, and toxic industrial atmosphere before it reaches the lungs — near-universal among Mechanicus adepts who spend their working lives on a forge-world's surface.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Filter Lungs (B55), 5 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"base_points": 5
		},
		{
			"id": "tHzu2CIo8DmPZPgIr",
			"name": "High Pain Threshold",
			"reference": "B59",
			"local_notes": "Lore: What remains of a Servitor's nervous system has been surgically and chemically dulled well past the point of registering ordinary pain.\n\nDesign: Basic Set High Pain Threshold (B59), 10 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": 10
		},
		{
			"id": "tbSGErSxszqc15-Gt",
			"name": "Injury Tolerance (No Blood)",
			"reference": "B61",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Heavy circulatory augmentation and replacement organs leave a Servitor largely unaffected by the bleeding-out effects that would drop an ordinary wounded human.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Injury Tolerance (No Blood) (B61), 5 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": 5
		},
		{
			"id": "Tsckx2fE6PdwSvlym",
			"name": "Servitor Lobotomy (Neural Excision)",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The surgical and chemical process that turns a criminal, debtor, or unfit citizen into a Servitor: swathes of the frontal cortex and speech centers are excised or chemically silenced, leaving a body that follows binharic command-cant and simple standing orders with total, uncomplaining obedience and nothing recognizable as a person behind the eyes.\n\nDesign: Slave Mentality (B154, -40, cannot disobey or act against orders) + Low Empathy (B142, -20, cannot read or care about others' feelings) + Cannot Speak (B145, -25, mute but for binharic response codes) = -85 points. Reduced IQ itself is bought on the character sheet (an attribute purchase, not an implant trait) — see Adeptus Mechanicus/Templates/Combat Servitor.gct for a worked example.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus",
				"Servitor"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "txNcYOpgxd1X1geNt",
					"name": "Slave Mentality",
					"reference": "B154",
					"base_points": -40
				},
				{
					"id": "t6ZuCiiCdlEgcLGbx",
					"name": "Low Empathy",
					"reference": "B142",
					"base_points": -20
				},
				{
					"id": "tc85B4vBpJyDPxcAA",
					"name": "Cannot Speak (Mute)",
					"reference": "B145",
					"local_notes": "Some Servitor patterns retain a handful of vox-triggered stock responses at the GM's discretion; treat this as flavor, not a mechanical exception.",
					"base_points": -25
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tHv38aq5wN8vfbAaR",
			"name": "Duty (Adeptus Mechanicus)",
			"reference": "B133",
			"local_notes": "Overridden to -15: a Combat Servitor's entire existence is service, with none of an ordained adept's remaining autonomy to soften it.\n\nLore: A sworn Tech-Priest, Enginseer, or Skitarii answers first to their Forge World and its Fabricator-General, not to any Guard officer or Administratum functionary they happen to be attached to — a binding, frequent, but not universally life-threatening obligation (unlike a Guardsman's), since a Mechanicus posting is at least as often archival or industrial as it is a battlefield one.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Duty (B133), fairly frequent but not \"almost always hazardous\" the way Duty (Astra Militarum) is (Imperium/Traits/ Imperial Traits.adq) — pegged one tier below that entry, at -10, to reflect the Priesthood's broader range of postings. A Skitarii or a field-attached Enginseer/Techmarine should reasonably use -15 instead; -10 is this template's baseline for a workshop- or forge-based adept.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Social",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"base_points": -15
		},
		{
			"id": "txRLIWfnYhgEgTsdQ",
			"name": "Social Stigma (Valuable Property)",
			"reference": "B156",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Servitor is Mechanicus property in exactly the legal sense the words imply: requisitioned, inventoried, and disposed of at need, with no standing to be treated otherwise anywhere in the Imperium.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Social Stigma (Valuable Property) (B156), -10.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Social",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -10
		}
	],
	"skills": [
		{
			"id": "sRodSGWZNKznT_i-L",
			"name": "Gunner",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The single combat routine most Combat Servitors are conditioned to execute, over and over, without variation.\n\nDesign: DX+2 (11) for 8 points, Average (B170).",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
